## Copilot

The application-readiness feature. **No endpoint in this group returns an eligibility decision.** Readiness is computed, never generated.

### Extraction and confirmation

#### `POST /api/copilot/extract`

Extract allowlisted fields from supplied document text.

```jsonc
{
  "documentText": "string",   // raw text of the document
  "sessionId": "string?",     // reused only if it already exists (anti-fixation)
  "documentId": "string?"
}
```

Returns extracted fields, each carrying `page`, `bbox`, `sourceDocId`, a confidence level, and a source snippet.

#### `POST /api/copilot/rag-extract`

Document *upload* variant, defined in `src/routes/ragExtract.ts`. Accepts either:

- `multipart/form-data` — `{ file: File, sessionId?: string }`
- `application/json` — `{ documentText, sessionId?, documentId? }`

Pipeline: parse to text (`pdf-parse` v2 for PDFs, `mammoth` for DOCX, vision for images) → sliding-window chunk if over threshold → embed chunks with `text-embedding-3-small` → cosine-similarity retrieval of top-K context → LLM field extraction under the same allowlist and security constraints as `/extract`.

**Constraints.** Multer memory storage only — nothing is written to disk. 10 MB file limit. MIME allowlist. Raw document text is never persisted to the session.

Returns the same JSON shape as `/copilot/extract`, so downstream stages are unchanged.

#### `POST /api/copilot/confirm`

Renter confirms or corrects the extracted values. Nothing proceeds on unconfirmed data.

```jsonc
{ "sessionId": "string", "confirmedFields": { }, "consent": true }
```

Consent is recorded as an action in the consent log — never with raw document text.

### Calculation

#### `POST /api/copilot/annualize`

```jsonc
{ "amount": 1200, "frequency": "biweekly", "householdSize": 3 }
```

Deterministic. Multiplies by the frequency table (`weekly` ×52, `biweekly` ×26, `semimonthly` ×24, `monthly` ×12, `annual` ×1), then compares against the frozen FY 2026 Boston MTSP 60% threshold.

Returns a comparison of `below_or_equal` | `above` | `no_frozen_threshold`. Household size above 8 always returns `no_frozen_threshold`.

### Rules

#### `POST /api/copilot/rules`

```jsonc
{ "question": "string", "householdSize": 3 }
```

Answers from the frozen corpus. Every answer carries `rule_id`, authority tier, effective date, and source URL. Questions matching a refusal category are declined with the governing rule cited — see [SAFETY.md](SAFETY.md).

#### `GET /api/copilot/rules/corpus`

The full 11-rule corpus: `HUD-MTSP-001..003`, `HUD-DATA-001`, `HUD-GEO-001`, `FED-LIHTC-001`, `FED-MONITOR-001`, `CH-INCOME-001`, `CH-READINESS-001`, `CH-SAFETY-001`, `CH-DECISION-001`.

#### `GET /api/copilot/mtsp`

The frozen FY 2026 MTSP threshold table.

#### `GET /api/copilot/qa` · `GET /api/copilot/qa/:qaId`

The curated question-and-answer set, listed and individually addressable.

### Checklist and packet

#### `GET /api/copilot/checklist?sessionId=...`

The document checklist. When a `sessionId` is supplied, item statuses are auto-populated from Stage 1 extraction evidence and each auto-detected item is marked with its detection source.

#### `GET /api/copilot/checklists` · `GET /api/copilot/checklists/:householdId`

Checklist templates, listed and by household.

#### `POST /api/copilot/packet`

```jsonc
{
  "sessionId": "string",
  "itemStatuses": { },
  "householdSize": 3,
  "detectionSources": { }
}
```

Assembles the packet and computes readiness automatically. Returns `readinessStatus` (`READY_TO_REVIEW` | `NEEDS_REVIEW`) plus a `reviewReasons` array.

Reason codes are derived from session document evidence — document type, document date, and per-document annualized income variance over 5% — never from checklist item labels. Granular codes include `PAY_STUB_TOTAL_CONFLICT`, `EMPLOYMENT_LETTER_EXPIRED`, and `GIG_INCOME_UNCORROBORATED`. `MISSING_REQUIRED_DOCUMENT`, `DOCUMENT_EXPIRED` and `NO_FROZEN_THRESHOLD` act as fallbacks.

Governed by `CH-READINESS-001` against the frozen date 2026-07-18 with a 60-day currency window.

#### `POST /api/copilot/submission`

```jsonc
{ "sessionId": "string", "householdId": "string", "householdSize": 3, "itemStatuses": { } }
```

Returns the schema-conformant submission object:

```jsonc
{
  "household_id": "string",
  "annualized_income": 0,
  "comparison": "below_or_equal | above | no_frozen_threshold",
  "readiness_status": "READY_TO_REVIEW | NEEDS_REVIEW",
  "review_reasons": [],
  "citations": []
}
```

### Feedback and session control

#### `POST /api/copilot/feedback`

```jsonc
{ "sessionId": "string", "question": "string", "rating": 1, "deterministic": true, "abstained": false }
```

#### `GET /api/copilot/feedback/stats`

Aggregate feedback statistics.

#### `GET /api/copilot/adversarial`

The adversarial test-case set covering all safety pattern categories.

#### `DELETE /api/copilot/session/:sessionId`

Renter-triggered session deletion. Sessions also expire automatically after a 30-minute TTL.

